From e391e61c0f83e0bf96b417a06d741415fdc1403e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 19:24:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/8] Typer: make memberskip skip when applies only reads
 memoized types

An extension that does not declare the looked-up name is skipped iff its
extendee type is memoized and either the match fails at the root (distinct
nominal heads or heads of different kinds) or the types of all givens
visible from the scope of use are memoized. In both cases applies() has no
effect beyond fresh variables and cache fills, so unlike names this does
not change the order in which extendees and givens are first evaluated.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011CH6tJP7hLkrpGFxEq7K6r
